{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:07:21Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 82, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Write", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NCcvQ9c6AeSgWhenh7GyAv", "input": {"file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/spec.md", "content": "# Spec: Edit a task title\n\nTaiga #2\n\n## Triage\n\n**Feature** \u2014 net-new capability, no existing behaviour changes. Single\ncohesive cycle: one new backend route plus the frontend UI to drive it. Does\nnot span enough architectural layers to warrant splitting (compare: Taiga #1\nwas frontend-only; this one adds one backend route + one store method + one\ncomponent's edit state \u2014 normal size for one cycle).\n\n## Goal\n\nLet someone fix a mistyped task title in place, without deleting and\nre-creating the task.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. **Enter edit mode.** Given a task in the list, when the user activates\n   editing on it, then the title is replaced with an editable input\n   pre-filled with the task's current title.\n2. **Save a valid edit.** Given a task in edit mode, when the user submits a\n   new title that is non-empty after trimming, then the task's title is\n   updated, the change is persisted (still present after a page reload), and\n   edit mode closes showing the new title.\n3. **Cancel discards changes.** Given a task in edit mode with a modified\n   draft, when the user cancels, then the title reverts to its original\n   value, no save request is sent, and edit mode closes.\n4. **Empty title is rejected, not saved.** Given a task in edit mode, when\n   the user submits a title that is empty or whitespace-only, then the save\n   is rejected: the task's title is unchanged (never blanked), the user gets\n   visible feedback that the title can't be empty, and they remain able to\n   correct it without having lost their place.\n5. **Oversized title is rejected.** Given a task in edit mode, when the user\n   submits a title over 200 characters (the existing `TaskIn` limit used for\n   create), then the save is rejected the same way create rejects it today,\n   and the task's title is unchanged.\n6. **Backend: successful update.** Given an existing task, when\n   `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}` is called with `{\"title\": \"<1-200 chars>\"}`, then\n   it returns `200` with the updated `Task`, and a subsequent `GET\n   /api/tasks` reflects the new title.\n7. **Backend: missing task.** Given no task with that id, when `PATCH\n   /api/tasks/{id}` is called, then it returns `404`.\n8. **Backend: empty title.** Given an existing task, when `PATCH\n   /api/tasks/{id}` is called with `{\"title\": \"\"}`, then it returns `422`\n   and the stored title is unchanged.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No edit history or undo beyond the in-progress cancel.\n- No multi-field bulk edit, no editing multiple tasks' titles at once.\n- No new concurrency/conflict resolution beyond what already exists \u2014 a save\n  against a task deleted by someone else surfaces as a `404` through the\n  existing error banner (`App.jsx`'s `run()` \u2192 `setError`), same as\n  completing or deleting an already-gone task does today.\n- No character counter or other new max-length UI beyond reusing the\n  existing 200-char backend validation.\n\n## Affected areas\n\n- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 add `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}` route (mirrors\n  the existing `POST /api/tasks/{task_id}/done` route shape at lines 32-37).\n- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 add `TaskStore.set_title(task_id, title)`,\n  mirroring `set_done` (lines 30-35).\n- `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 no change; the new route reuses `TaskIn`\n  (line 5-6) for its request body, same validation as create.\n- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \u2014 add tests for the new route, following the\n  existing `client` fixture pattern (success, 404, 422 empty title).\n- `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 add `updateTask(id, title)` issuing a `PATCH`,\n  next to `completeTask`/`deleteTask` (lines 20-21).\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 add per-task edit-mode state and\n  the editable-input UI (currently renders `task-title` as plain text at\n  line 15).\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 add an `onEdit` handler wired through the\n  existing `run()` helper (lines 33-40), same pattern as `onComplete` /\n  `onDelete` (lines 54-55).\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 styles for the edit input and its save/cancel\n  controls, extending the existing `.task` rules (lines 30-35).\n\nExact trigger affordance, save/cancel control placement, and any\nkeyboard-shortcut behavior (e.g. Enter/Escape) beyond the input's minimum\nsave/cancel actions are the ux-designer's call, not fixed here.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- Empty title submitted \u2192 rejected, task unchanged (AC4).\n- Whitespace-only title (`\"   \"`) \u2192 trimmed before validation, treated the\n  same as empty (AC4). Trimming happens client-side before the request is\n  sent, same as `AddTask.jsx` already does for creation (line 8).\n- Cancel with a modified draft \u2192 reverts, no request sent (AC3).\n- Save with the draft identical to the original title \u2192 treated as a normal\n  save (a `PATCH` is still sent); not special-cased, since it's harmless and\n  idempotent in this in-memory store.\n- Title over 200 characters \u2192 rejected by existing `TaskIn` validation\n  (AC5), surfaced to the user rather than failing silently.\n- Task deleted by another client while being edited \u2192 save fails with `404`,\n  surfaced through the existing error banner (see Non-goals).\n- Editing a task that is already marked `done` \u2192 allowed; nothing in the\n  request restricts editing to open tasks only (see Open Questions).\n- Two tasks edited \"at once\" \u2192 out of scope for the UI to prevent explicitly,\n  but see Open Questions for the assumed default.\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. **Can a `done` task's title still be edited?** Assumption: yes \u2014 nothing\n   in the request excludes completed tasks, and there's no separate\n   \"locked\" state today. Override if done tasks should be read-only.\n2. **Can more than one task be in edit mode at the same time?** Assumption:\n   no \u2014 only one task edits at a time (opening edit on a second task closes\n   the first, discarding its unsaved draft, same as a \"cancel\"). Keeps the\n   interaction and state simple, and matches a single-column list UI.\n   Override if simultaneous multi-edit is wanted.\n"}, "session_id": "852774c2-c0ba-46f2-a2f0-7bd73cc17f62"}}
