{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:33:16Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 20, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Spec: Filter tasks by done state\n2\t\n3\tTaiga #1\n4\t\n5\t## Triage\n6\t\n7\t**Feature** \u2014 net-new capability, no existing behaviour changes.\n8\t\n9\t## Goal\n10\t\n11\tLet someone with a long task list show only the tasks they still need to do,\n12\tor only the ones they've finished, so the list stays useful as it grows.\n13\t\n14\t## Acceptance criteria\n15\t\n16\t1. Given the task list, when the page loads with no prior filter choice made,\n17\t   then all tasks are shown (filter = **All**) \u2014 see Open Question 1 for why\n18\t   this is the default.\n19\t2. Given tasks in a mix of done/not-done states, when the user selects\n20\t   **Open**, then only tasks with `done: false` are shown.\n21\t3. Given tasks in a mix of done/not-done states, when the user selects\n22\t   **Done**, then only tasks with `done: true` are shown.\n23\t4. Given any filter is selected, when the user selects **All**, then every\n24\t   task is shown regardless of `done` state.\n25\t5. Given a filter is active, the currently selected filter is visually\n26\t   distinguishable from the other two options (exact treatment is the\n27\t   ux-designer's call).\n28\t6. Given filter = **Open** is active, when a new task is added, then it\n29\t   appears in the list (new tasks are always `done: false`, so they match\n30\t   Open and All, and are correctly hidden under Done).\n31\t7. Given filter = **Done** is active, when a new task is added, then it does\n32\t   **not** appear in the list until it is marked done.\n33\t8. Given filter = **Open** is active, when an existing visible task is marked\n34\t   done, then it immediately disappears from the Open view (it no longer\n35\t   matches the filter).\n36\t9. Given filter = **Done** is active, when a task is marked done elsewhere\n37\t   accessible under this filter, then it immediately appears.\n38\t10. Given a filter is active, when a task is deleted, then it is removed from\n39\t    the list the same way it is today, regardless of which filter is active.\n40\t11. The filter choice does not reset on its own after an add/complete/delete\n41\t    action \u2014 `App.jsx`'s existing `refresh()` re-fetches the task list on\n42\t    every action, and the chosen filter must keep applying to the freshly\n43\t    fetched data rather than reverting to All.\n44\t12. Given filter = **Open** and every task is done (or there are zero tasks),\n45\t    then the list area shows an explicit empty state for that filter rather\n46\t    than silently rendering nothing.\n47\t13. Given filter = **Done** and no task is done yet, then the list area shows\n48\t    an explicit empty state for that filter.\n49\t\n50\t## Non-goals\n51\t\n52\t- No backend/API changes. `GET /api/tasks` already returns `done` on every\n53\t  task; filtering happens entirely client-side against data already fetched.\n54\t  `frontend/src/api.js` and everything under `backend/` are untouched.\n55\t- No persistence of the filter choice across a full page reload (no\n56\t  `localStorage`, no URL query param). It resets to All on reload \u2014 see Open\n57\t  Question 2.\n58\t- No counts/badges next to each filter option (e.g. \"Open (3)\"). Not asked\n59\t  for; would be a natural follow-up, not in scope here.\n60\t- No additional filter dimensions (by title text, by date). Done-state only,\n61\t  as three options: All / Open / Done.\n62\t\n63\t## Affected areas\n64\t\n65\t- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 currently fetches `tasks` and passes the full\n66\t  array straight to `TaskList`. Needs to hold the active filter as state and\n67\t  derive the filtered array before passing it down (or pass both `tasks` and\n68\t  `filter` down, ux-designer/developer's call on where the derivation lives).\n69\t- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 currently renders one hardcoded\n70\t  empty state (`\"Nothing to do yet.\"`) regardless of context. Needs\n71\t  filter-aware empty-state copy per acceptance criteria 12\u201313.\n72\t- A new component under `frontend/src/components/` for the filter control\n73\t  itself (e.g. a segmented control or button group), per this project's \"one\n74\t  component per file\" convention. Exact name/shape is the ux-designer's call.\n75\t- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 new styles for the filter control and its active\n76\t  state.\n77\t- Not affected: `backend/app/main.py`, `backend/app/models.py`,\n78\t  `backend/app/store.py`, `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 no server-side filtering,\n79\t  no new endpoints, no schema change.\n80\t\n81\t## Edge cases\n82\t\n83\t- Zero tasks exist at all, filter = All: existing `\"Nothing to do yet.\"`\n84\t  copy applies unchanged.\n85\t- Zero tasks exist at all, filter = Open or Done: same empty state as \"all\n86\t  tasks filtered out\" (criteria 12\u201313) \u2014 no need to distinguish \"no tasks\"\n87\t  from \"no tasks matching filter.\"\n88\t- All tasks are done, filter = Open \u2192 empty state (criterion 12).\n89\t- No tasks are done, filter = Done \u2192 empty state (criterion 13).\n90\t- Filter interacts with the existing `loading` state in `App.jsx`: the\n91\t  loading message takes precedence; filter controls may render but there's\n92\t  nothing to filter yet.\n93\t- Filter interacts with the existing `error` state: unaffected \u2014 error\n94\t  banner behaviour is unchanged, filter controls remain visible and usable.\n95\t- Deleting the last task visible under the current filter must show that\n96\t  filter's empty state, not silently blank the list and not auto-switch back\n97\t  to All.\n98\t- Rapid switching between filter options: pure synchronous client-side\n99\t  state, no request involved, so no race condition to guard against.\n100\t\n101\t## Open questions\n102\t\n103\t1. **Default filter on load.** Assumption: **All**. This matches current\n104\t   behaviour exactly (nothing is hidden that isn't hidden today), so shipping\n105\t   this feature can't itself hide a task from someone who hasn't touched the\n106\t   new control yet. Proceeding on this assumption.\n107\t2. **Should the filter choice survive a page reload?** Assumption: **No** \u2014\n108\t   resets to All each load, matching the non-goal above. The request didn't\n109\t   ask for persistence, and adding it would touch either `localStorage` or\n110\t   routing, which is more surface than this feature needs. Proceeding on this\n111\t   assumption; flag to the user if they'd actually like it remembered.\n112\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FHbGPwtBd1vbqtXyQnC9y1", "session_id": "7316b1e8-1a1b-45f3-8c7b-90f2dd28a686"}}
