{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:33:16Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 23, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Design: Filter tasks by done state\n2\t\n3\tSource: `docs/spec.md` (Taiga #1)\n4\t\n5\t## Summary of decisions\n6\t\n7\t- New component `frontend/src/components/TaskFilter.jsx` \u2014 a 3-segment\n8\t  toggle group (All / Open / Done), styled as a single bordered pill split\n9\t  into three buttons, matching this project's existing plain-button look.\n10\t- Active segment: filled dark background (`#16191c`) with white text \u2014\n11\t  reuses the app's existing near-black text color as a background instead of\n12\t  introducing a new accent hue. Computed contrast 17.65:1 (see below).\n13\t- Filtering logic (deriving the visible subset from `tasks` + `filter`)\n14\t  lives in `App.jsx`, next to where `tasks` state already lives. `TaskList`\n15\t  receives the already-filtered array plus the raw `filter` value (used only\n16\t  to pick empty-state copy, not to filter).\n17\t- Filter control renders unconditionally, positioned between the error\n18\t  banner and the loading/list area, so the layout doesn't shift when loading\n19\t  resolves and so it stays visible+usable during the error state (edge case\n20\t  in spec).\n21\t- No new focus styles, no new UI library, no icon set. Plain `<button>`\n22\t  elements get the browser's native focus ring, exactly like `AddTask`'s and\n23\t  `TaskList`'s existing buttons.\n24\t\n25\t## Component tree change\n26\t\n27\t```\n28\tApp.jsx\n29\t\u251c\u2500 h1 \"Tasks\"\n30\t\u251c\u2500 AddTask               (unchanged)\n31\t\u251c\u2500 error banner          (unchanged)\n32\t\u251c\u2500 TaskFilter             \u2190 NEW \u2014 always rendered once tasks have loaded state exists\n33\t\u2514\u2500 loading | TaskList\n34\t             \u2514\u2500 TaskList  (empty-state copy now filter-aware)\n35\t```\n36\t\n37\t## New component: `frontend/src/components/TaskFilter.jsx`\n38\t\n39\tProps: `{ value, onChange }` \u2014 `value` is `'all' | 'open' | 'done'`,\n40\t`onChange(nextValue)` is called on click. Mirrors the `onAdd`/`onComplete`\n41\tcallback-prop pattern already used by `AddTask`/`TaskList`.\n42\t\n43\t```jsx\n44\texport default function TaskFilter({ value, onChange }) {\n45\t  const options = [\n46\t    { value: 'all', label: 'All' },\n47\t    { value: 'open', label: 'Open' },\n48\t    { value: 'done', label: 'Done' },\n49\t  ]\n50\t  return (\n51\t    <div className=\"task-filter\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Filter tasks\">\n52\t      {options.map((opt) => (\n53\t        <button\n54\t          key={opt.value}\n55\t          type=\"button\"\n56\t          className={opt.value === value ? 'filter-option active' : 'filter-option'}\n57\t          aria-pressed={opt.value === value}\n58\t          onClick={() => onChange(opt.value)}\n59\t        >\n60\t          {opt.label}\n61\t        </button>\n62\t      ))}\n63\t    </div>\n64\t  )\n65\t}\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\tWhy plain toggle buttons (`role=\"group\"` + `aria-pressed`) rather than a\n69\tnative `role=\"radiogroup\"`/`role=\"radio\"` pattern: a radiogroup implies\n70\tarrow-key navigation between options, which is a keyboard-interaction\n71\tpattern this codebase doesn't have anywhere else (`AddTask`, `TaskList` use\n72\tonly native tab order and Enter/Space activation). `aria-pressed` toggle\n73\tbuttons are simpler, still communicate the selected state to assistive\n74\ttech, and are consistent with how much interaction complexity the rest of\n75\tthe app has. Tab order is left-to-right through All \u2192 Open \u2192 Done, same as\n76\tvisual order, no `tabIndex` needed.\n77\t\n78\t## `App.jsx` changes\n79\t\n80\t- Add `const [filter, setFilter] = useState('all')`.\n81\t- Derive the visible list: `const visibleTasks = tasks.filter(t => filter === 'all' ? true : filter === 'open' ? !t.done : t.done)`. Plain filter, no memoization needed \u2014 the list sizes here don't warrant it and nothing else in this codebase memoizes.\n82\t- `filter` state is untouched by `refresh()`, so it survives every\n83\t  add/complete/delete cycle automatically (AC 11) \u2014 `refresh()` only ever\n84\t  calls `setTasks`, never `setFilter`.\n85\t- Render order: `AddTask` \u2192 error banner (unchanged) \u2192 `<TaskFilter value={filter} onChange={setFilter} />` \u2192 `loading ? <p className=\"loading\">\u2026</p> : <TaskList tasks={visibleTasks} filter={filter} onComplete={...} onDelete={...} />`.\n86\t- `TaskFilter` renders even while `loading` is true (per spec edge case:\n87\t  \"filter controls may render but there's nothing to filter yet\"). This\n88\t  keeps the header/control area layout stable across the loading\u2192loaded\n89\t  transition instead of popping in after fetch completes.\n90\t\n91\t## `TaskList.jsx` changes\n92\t\n93\tEmpty-state copy becomes a 3-way lookup keyed by the incoming `filter` prop,\n94\tparallel in tone to the existing message:\n95\t\n96\t```jsx\n97\tconst EMPTY_COPY = {\n98\t  all: 'Nothing to do yet.',\n99\t  open: 'Nothing open right now.',\n100\t  done: 'Nothing done yet.',\n101\t}\n102\t\n103\texport default function TaskList({ tasks, filter, onComplete, onDelete }) {\n104\t  if (tasks.length === 0) {\n105\t    return <p className=\"empty\">{EMPTY_COPY[filter]}</p>\n106\t  }\n107\t  // ...unchanged rendering of the <ul> below\n108\t}\n109\t```\n110\t\n111\t`tasks` here is already the filtered array from `App.jsx` \u2014 `TaskList` does\n112\tnot re-derive anything, it only picks copy. Per-item rendering (`task`,\n113\t`task.done` line-through, Complete/Delete buttons) is entirely unchanged;\n114\tfiltering never touches how an individual task renders, only which ones are\n115\tpresent in the array.\n116\t\n117\t## `App.css` additions\n118\t\n119\t```css\n120\t.task-filter {\n121\t  display: inline-flex;\n122\t  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n123\t  border-radius: 6px;\n124\t  overflow: hidden;\n125\t  margin-bottom: 1.2rem;\n126\t}\n127\t.filter-option {\n128\t  border: none;\n129\t  border-radius: 0;\n130\t  background: #fff;\n131\t  padding: 0.45rem 0.9rem;\n132\t  font: inherit;\n133\t  color: #16191c;\n134\t  cursor: pointer;\n135\t}\n136\t.filter-option + .filter-option { border-left: 1px solid #ccd2d6; }\n137\t.filter-option.active { background: #16191c; color: #fff; }\n138\t```\n139\t\n140\tFollows the existing button styling (`border-radius: 5px`-ish, `#ccd2d6`\n141\tborders, `#fff` background) but merges the three segments into one bordered\n142\tgroup instead of three separate floating buttons, which is the standard\n143\tsegmented-control shape and reads clearly as \"one control, three settings\"\n144\trather than three unrelated actions. No `:hover` override is added \u2014\n145\texisting buttons in this app don't define one either (`button` has no hover\n146\trule in `App.css` today), so `TaskFilter` doesn't invent a new pattern.\n147\t\n148\t## States\n149\t\n150\t### Loading (filter renders, nothing to filter yet)\n151\t\n152\t```\n153\tTasks\n154\t[ Add-task input............] [Add]\n155\t[ All ][ Open ][ Done ]\n156\tLoading\u2026\n157\t```\n158\t\n159\t`All` is active (default per AC 1). Clicking `Open`/`Done` here is harmless\n160\t\u2014 `setFilter` fires, `visibleTasks` recomputes against `tasks = []`, so\n161\tnothing visibly changes until `refresh()` resolves and the real list\n162\trenders already filtered correctly.\n163\t\n164\t### Error (filter stays visible and usable \u2014 spec edge case)\n165\t\n166\t```\n167\tTasks\n168\t[ Add-task input............] [Add]\n169\t\u26a0 Could not reach the server.\n170\t[ All ][ Open ][ Done ]\n171\tLoading\u2026 / <TaskList>\n172\t```\n173\t\n174\tUnchanged error banner behavior; `TaskFilter` is just another sibling, not\n175\tgated on `error`.\n176\t\n177\t### Populated \u2014 All (default, AC 1)\n178\t\n179\t```\n180\t[\u25a0All][ Open ][ Done ]\n181\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n182\t\u2502 Buy milk                [Done][Delete]\n183\t\u2502 ~~Walk the dog~~            [Delete]\n184\t\u2502 Finish report            [Done][Delete]\n185\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n186\t```\n187\t(`\u25a0` denotes the filled/active segment; `~~ ~~` denotes the existing\n188\tstrikethrough treatment for done items.) Both done and not-done tasks\n189\tappear \u2014 unchanged from current behavior.\n190\t\n191\t### Populated \u2014 Open (AC 2, 6, 8)\n192\t\n193\t```\n194\t[ All ][\u25a0Open][ Done ]\n195\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n196\t\u2502 Buy milk                [Done][Delete]\n197\t\u2502 Finish report            [Done][Delete]\n198\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n199\t```\n200\tOnly `done: false` tasks. A newly added task appears here immediately (AC\n201\t6). Marking a visible task done removes it from this view on the next\n202\t`refresh()` (AC 8).\n203\t\n204\t### Populated \u2014 Done (AC 3, 7, 9)\n205\t\n206\t```\n207\t[ All ][ Open ][\u25a0Done]\n208\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n209\t\u2502 ~~Walk the dog~~            [Delete]\n210\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n211\t```\n212\tOnly `done: true` tasks. Newly added tasks never appear here until\n213\tcompleted (AC 7); a task completed elsewhere appears here on next refresh\n214\t(AC 9). Note: completed tasks lose their `[Done]` button (existing\n215\t`TaskList` behavior, unchanged) \u2014 only `[Delete]` remains, matching current\n216\tproduction behavior for done items under All today.\n217\t\n218\t### Empty \u2014 All, zero tasks (unchanged)\n219\t\n220\t```\n221\t[\u25a0All][ Open ][ Done ]\n222\tNothing to do yet.\n223\t```\n224\t\n225\t### Empty \u2014 Open, all done or zero tasks (AC 12)\n226\t\n227\t```\n228\t[ All ][\u25a0Open][ Done ]\n229\tNothing open right now.\n230\t```\n231\t\n232\t### Empty \u2014 Done, none done yet (AC 13)\n233\t\n234\t```\n235\t[ All ][ Open ][\u25a0Done]\n236\tNothing done yet.\n237\t```\n238\t\n239\t### Interactive states\n240\t\n241\t- **Default (unselected) segment:** white background, `#16191c` text,\n242\t  `#ccd2d6` 1px border/divider \u2014 identical visual weight to existing\n243\t  `Done`/`Delete`/`Add` buttons.\n244\t- **Active (selected) segment:** `#16191c` background, `#fff` text. No\n245\t  border change needed since the fill itself communicates state.\n246\t- **Hover:** no custom rule (matches existing app-wide absence of hover\n247\t  styling); browser default (cursor: pointer, already set).\n248\t- **Focus:** native browser focus ring (no custom `:focus-visible` rule),\n249\t  consistent with every other interactive element in this app.\n250\t- **Disabled:** not used. Every option remains clickable at all times,\n251\t  including clicking the already-active option (a harmless no-op re-set),\n252\t  since the spec has no case where a filter option should be unavailable.\n253\t\n254\t## Accessibility\n255\t\n256\t- Target size: `.filter-option` padding (`0.45rem 0.9rem` \u2248 7px vertical +\n257\t  1px border) yields roughly the same ~34\u201336px tap height as the existing\n258\t  `Add`/`Done`/`Delete` buttons in this app. This is under the 44px\n259\t  ideal, but it matches what's already shipped elsewhere in the same\n260\t  screen \u2014 not a regression introduced by this feature. Flagging as a\n261\t  possible follow-up if the project wants to raise touch targets\n262\t  app-wide, out of scope here.\n263\t- Contrast, active segment (`#fff` text on `#16191c` background): computed\n264\t  relative luminance of `#16191c` \u2248 0.00948, of white = 1.0 \u2192\n265\t  ratio = (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.00948 + 0.05) \u2248 **17.65:1**. Passes both the\n266\t  4.5:1 text minimum and 3:1 non-text/UI-boundary minimum by a wide margin.\n267\t- Contrast, inactive segment (`#16191c` text on `#fff`): same pairing the\n268\t  rest of the app already relies on for body text \u2014 same \u224817.65:1 ratio,\n269\t  already implicitly validated by existing production UI.\n270\t- `role=\"group\"` + `aria-label=\"Filter tasks\"` on the container, and\n271\t  `aria-pressed` per button, so a screen reader announces \"Filter tasks,\n272\t  group\" then \"All, toggle button, pressed\" (or not pressed) per option.\n273\t- Tab order: input \u2192 Add \u2192 All \u2192 Open \u2192 Done \u2192 (per-task Done/Delete\n274\t  buttons), left-to-right, no `tabIndex` overrides.\n275\t\n276\t## Acceptance criteria traceability\n277\t\n278\t| AC | Design element |\n279\t|----|-----------------|\n280\t| 1 | `App.jsx` `useState('all')` default; \"Populated \u2014 All\" state |\n281\t| 2 | `visibleTasks` filter `!t.done`; \"Populated \u2014 Open\" state |\n282\t| 3 | `visibleTasks` filter `t.done`; \"Populated \u2014 Done\" state |\n283\t| 4 | Clicking `All` segment calls `onChange('all')`, resets derivation |\n284\t| 5 | `.filter-option.active` fill treatment, see Interactive states |\n285\t| 6 | `filter` state untouched by `refresh()`; Open view re-derives from new `tasks` |\n286\t| 7 | Same \u2014 Done view excludes new (`done:false`) tasks until completed |\n287\t| 8 | Re-derivation on next `refresh()` after `onComplete` |\n288\t| 9 | Same, Done direction |\n289\t| 10 | Delete unaffected \u2014 `TaskList`'s existing delete button/behavior untouched |\n290\t| 11 | `filter` state lives in `App.jsx`, never reset by `refresh()`/`run()` |\n291\t| 12 | \"Empty \u2014 Open\" state, `EMPTY_COPY.open` |\n292\t| 13 | \"Empty \u2014 Done\" state, `EMPTY_COPY.done` |\n293\t\n294\t## Non-goals honored\n295\t\n296\tNo new colors/hues beyond the existing palette, no counts/badges on\n297\toptions, no persistence mechanism, no additional filter dimensions \u2014\n298\tmatches spec's non-goals section exactly.\n299\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01YB9dGc1NcfwbypwPx26jkQ", "session_id": "7316b1e8-1a1b-45f3-8c7b-90f2dd28a686"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:33:16Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 24, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t\"\"\"Route wiring only -- behaviour lives in store.py.\"\"\"\n2\tfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\n3\tfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n4\t\n5\tfrom .models import Task, TaskIn\n6\tfrom .store import store\n7\t\n8\tapp = FastAPI(title=\"test-project\")\n9\t\n10\t# A regex, not a fixed list: the dev server is reached as both localhost and\n11\t# 127.0.0.1, and the e2e harness binds it to a free port rather than 5173, so\n12\t# a hardcoded origin silently blocks every write from the browser while GETs\n13\t# keep working -- which reads as \"adding a task does nothing\".\n14\tapp.add_middleware(\n15\t    CORSMiddleware,\n16\t    allow_origin_regex=r\"http://(localhost|127\\.0\\.0\\.1):\\d+\",\n17\t    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n18\t    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n19\t)\n20\t\n21\t\n22\t@app.get(\"/api/tasks\", response_model=list[Task])\n23\tdef list_tasks() -> list[Task]:\n24\t    return store.list()\n25\t\n26\t\n27\t@app.post(\"/api/tasks\", response_model=Task, status_code=201)\n28\tdef create_task(payload: TaskIn) -> Task:\n29\t    return store.add(payload.title)\n30\t\n31\t\n32\t@app.post(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}/done\", response_model=Task)\n33\tdef complete_task(task_id: int) -> Task:\n34\t    task = store.set_done(task_id, True)\n35\t    if task is None:\n36\t        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"no such task\")\n37\t    return task\n38\t\n39\t\n40\t@app.delete(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}\", status_code=204)\n41\tdef delete_task(task_id: int) -> None:\n42\t    if not store.delete(task_id):\n43\t        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"no such task\")\n44\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VDexKyHF8gLiu1GwUZKiGe", "session_id": "7316b1e8-1a1b-45f3-8c7b-90f2dd28a686"}}
