{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:34:54Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 91, "kind": "message", "text": "I've triaged Taiga #3 as a **Feature** and written `docs/spec.md` (overwriting round 1's spec, per this pipeline's per-cycle `docs/` convention \u2014 round 1 is already merged per git log).\n\nSummary of the spec:\n\n- **Scope:** in-place title editing on an existing task row \u2014 enter edit mode, Save (persists via a new backend endpoint) or Cancel (reverts, no backend call), with empty/whitespace titles rejected client- and server-side.\n- **Backend:** new `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}` in `backend/app/main.py`, a new `update_title` method in `backend/app/store.py` (parallel to `set_done`), reusing the existing `TaskIn` model for validation \u2014 no schema change needed.\n- **Frontend:** `frontend/src/api.js` gets `updateTask`, `TaskList.jsx` gets per-row edit state (input + Save/Cancel), `App.jsx` wires an `onUpdate` callback the same way `onComplete`/`onDelete` already work.\n- **Two open questions**, both resolved with stated defaults rather than left open: exact edit-trigger UI (ux-designer's call, no new visual pattern) and the endpoint shape (`PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}`).\n- Explicitly **not** touching the create endpoint's existing whitespace-validation quirk, `done` state, or bulk editing.\n\nNot split into sub-specs \u2014 despite spanning backend+frontend, it's the natural shape of one small feature in this app, not a disproportionate cross-layer change.\n\nNext stage is **ux-designer**, to turn this into `docs/design.md`.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "7316b1e8-1a1b-45f3-8c7b-90f2dd28a686"}}
